{"cid:185460":{"key":"cid:185460","title":"Bilastine","compound":{"key":"cid:185460","cid":185460,"qid":"Q2902977","title":"Bilastine","iupac":"2-[4-[2-[4-[1-(2-ethoxyethyl)benzimidazol-2-yl]piperidin-1-yl]ethyl]phenyl]-2-methylpropanoic acid","wiki_url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bilastine","cas":"202189-78-4","iuphar":null,"drugbank":"DB11591; DB12481","chemspider":"161234","unii":"PA1123N395","kegg":null,"chebi":"135954","chembl":"CHEMBL1742423","pdb_ligand":null,"comptox":"DTXSID5057678","echa":"100.260.016","description":"chemical compound, antihistamine pharmaceutical substance","kind":null,"atc":"R06AX29","mesh":null,"uniprot":null,"ncbi_taxon":null,"gbif":null,"powo":null,"extra_at":"2026-11-08T19:46:28+00:00","eml":null,"smiles":"CCOCCN1C2=CC=CC=C2N=C1C3CCN(CC3)CCC4=CC=C(C=C4)C(C)(C)C(=O)O","chembl_phase":4.0,"first_approval":null,"bbw":0,"fda":0,"ema":1,"control":null,"reg_at":"2026-11-10T10:43:10+00:00"},"status":null,"pharm":[{"section":"Drug Indication","items":[{"section":"Drug Indication","text":"For symptomatic relief of nasal and non-nasal symptoms of seasonal rhinitis in patients 12 years of age and older and for symptomatic relief in chronic spontaneous urticaria in patients 18 years of age and older.","source":"DrugBank","url":"https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB11591","license_url":"https://www.drugbank.ca/legal/terms_of_use"},{"section":"Drug Indication","text":"FDA Label","source":"DrugBank","url":"https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB11591","license_url":"https://www.drugbank.ca/legal/terms_of_use"}]},{"section":"Drug Classes","items":[{"section":"Drug Classes","text":"Breast Feeding; Lactation; Milk, Human; Antihistamines; Nonsedating Antihistamines; Histamine Antagonists","source":"Drugs and Lactation Database (LactMed)","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/n/lactmed/bilastine/","license_url":"https://www.nlm.nih.gov/copyright.html"}]},{"section":"Pharmacodynamics","items":[{"section":"Pharmacodynamics","text":"Bilastine is an antiallergenic and acts to reduce allergic symptoms such as nasal congestion and urticaria.","source":"DrugBank","url":"https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB11591","license_url":"https://www.drugbank.ca/legal/terms_of_use"}]},{"section":"Mechanism of Action","items":[{"section":"Mechanism of Action","text":"Bilastine is a selective histamine H1 receptor antagonist (Ki = 64nM). During allergic response mast cells undergo degranulation which releases histamine and other subastances. By binding to and preventing activation of the H1 receptor, bilastine reduces the development of allergic symptoms due to the release of histamine from mast cells.","source":"DrugBank","url":"https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB11591","license_url":"https://www.drugbank.ca/legal/terms_of_use"}]},{"section":"Absorption, Distribution and Excretion","items":[{"section":"Absorption, Distribution and Excretion","text":"Bilastine has a Tmax of 1.13 h. The absolute bioavailability is 61%. No accumulation observed with daily dosing of 20-100 mg after 14 days. Cmax decreased by 25 % and 33% when taken with a low fat and high fat meal compared to fasted state. Administration with grapefruit juice decreased Cmax by 30%.","source":"DrugBank","url":"https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB11591","license_url":"https://www.drugbank.ca/legal/terms_of_use"},{"section":"Absorption, Distribution and Excretion","text":"Bilastine is mainly excreted in the feces (66.5%) with some excreted in the urine (28.3%). Nearly all is excreted as the parent compound.","source":"DrugBank","url":"https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB11591","license_url":"https://www.drugbank.ca/legal/terms_of_use"},{"section":"Absorption, Distribution and Excretion","text":"Bilastine has a total clearance is 9.20 L/h and a renal clearance of 8.7 L/h.","source":"DrugBank","url":"https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB11591","license_url":"https://www.drugbank.ca/legal/terms_of_use"}]},{"section":"Protein Binding","items":[{"section":"Protein Binding","text":"Bilastine is 84-90% bound to human plasma proteins.","source":"DrugBank","url":"https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB11591","license_url":"https://www.drugbank.ca/legal/terms_of_use"}]},{"section":"Metabolism/Metabolites","items":[{"section":"Metabolism/Metabolites","text":"Bilastine does not interact with the cytochrome P450 system and does not undergo significant metabolism in humans.","source":"DrugBank","url":"https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB11591","license_url":"https://www.drugbank.ca/legal/terms_of_use"}]},{"section":"Biological Half-Life","items":[{"section":"Biological Half-Life","text":"The mean half life of elimination is 14.5h.","source":"DrugBank","url":"https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB11591","license_url":"https://www.drugbank.ca/legal/terms_of_use"}]}],"safety":[{"section":"Effects During Pregnancy and Lactation","items":[{"section":"Effects During Pregnancy and Lactation","text":"◉ Summary of Use during Lactation Because no information is available on the use of bilastine during breastfeeding, an alternate drug may be preferred, especially while nursing a newborn or preterm infant. If it is used in a nursing mother, monitor the infant for sedation, poor feeding and poor weight gain. ◉ Effects in Breastfed Infants Relevant published information was not found as of the revision date. ◉ Effects on Lactation and Breastmilk Relevant published information was not found as of the revision date.","source":"Drugs and Lactation Database (LactMed)","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/n/lactmed/bilastine/"}]}],"manufacturing":[],"structure":true,"populations":{"child":{"label":"Suitable for children","count":7,"forms":[["Oral Solution",4],["Oro-dispersible tablet",3]]},"noswallow":{"label":"No tablet or capsule to swallow","count":7,"forms":[["Oral Solution",4],["Oro-dispersible tablet",3]]}},"reg":{"fda":0,"ema":1,"phase":4.0,"first_approval":null,"bbw":false,"control":null,"withdrawn":[],"reg_checked":true,"aware":null},"chem":{"props":{"key":"cid:185460","title":"Bilastine","prod